  "description": "POQZOO crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H64 Cl2 Dy5 N22 O18,4(C1 H4 O1),7(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.751-3.950 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.23-115.89°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C92H94ClDy5N22O30. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
